 440 km2, making it one of the smallest countries in the Caribbean. The country is mostly flat, with the highest points on Antigua being in the Shekerley Mountains and on Barbuda the Highlands. The country has a tropical savanna climate, with pockets of tropical monsoon in Antigua's southwest. Its most populated city is St. John's, followed by All Saints and Bolans. The sole settlement in Barbuda is Codrington. Most of the country resides in the Central Plain that stretches from St. John's to English Harbour.","description":"Country in the Lesser Antilles","thumbnailUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Flag_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg/330px-Flag_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg.png","canonicalUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antigua_and_Barbuda","revisionTimestamp":"2026-07-21T11:47:54Z"}},"trade":{"ok":false,"reason":"Comtrade HTTP 429 for reporter 28 flow X"},"weather":{"ok":true,"data":{"temperatureC":29.9,"windKph":25.7,"observedAt":"2026-08-02T19:30"}},"fx":{"ok":false,"reason":"XCD not covered by Frankfurter"},"famousPeople":{"ok":true,"data":[]},"overrides":{},"capturedAt":"2026-08-02T19:33:58.118Z"}